# TonyPi: earlyoom kills the biggest *optional* process before RAM runs out, so the Pi never livelocks on zram.
# (2026-10-29 the Pi froze with llama-server + several Claude Code sessions + harness Node/Hermes jobs.)
# Acts when available RAM AND free swap are both low: SIGTERM below 8 % / 40 %, SIGKILL below 4 % / 20 %.
# Robot core is never chosen; dev / harness jobs are chosen first; otherwise the largest (usually llama-server,
# which systemd restarts).
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-m 8,4 -s 40,20 -r 3600 --avoid '^(tonyd|tonypi-agent|tonypi-mcp|sshd|sshd-session|systemd|systemd-.*|init|NetworkManager|dbus-daemon)$' --prefer '^(node|pi|hermes|python|python3|pytest|uv|npm|cc1plus|ld|cmake|make)$'"
